        <div id="who" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Who Should Buy BodyTech, and Who Should Skip It
          </h2>

          <p>
            <strong>Buy the BodyTech isolate</strong> if you want a true whey isolate with a short label, you shop at The Vitamin Shoppe or can catch it on sale, and you are not drug tested. French Vanilla is the best flavored pick on the label, at 86% protein by weight. Buy the 3 lb or 5 lb tub, or use Auto Delivery, because the 1.5 lb tub at full price is where BodyTech stops being good value.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Buy Unflavored</strong> if you avoid artificial sweeteners, cook with protein or want the fewest ingredients possible. Two ingredients, 25 g of protein and 45 mg of sodium is hard to beat. It is a strong pick for pancakes, oats and smoothies, and our <a href="/best-unflavored-protein-powder/">best unflavored protein powder</a> guide ranks it against other plain options.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Buy Whey Tech Pro 24</strong> if you digest regular whey fine and want the cheapest protein BodyTech makes. In the 5 lb tub on Amazon it was about $1.35 per 25 g, which is hard to argue with. <strong>Skip BodyTech</strong> if you are a drug-tested athlete, if you want published heavy-metals data, or if you need a dairy-free protein. And skip the clear whey unless the juice-style format is the point, because it costs more per gram than the regular isolate at full price.
          </p>

          <p>
            Finally, check the date on the tub, especially if you buy a big one on sale. Whey stays good well past most people's usage window when stored sealed and dry, but our guide on <a href="/does-protein-powder-expire/">whether protein powder expires</a> explains what changes over time. People with kidney disease, those who are pregnant, and anyone with allergies or on medication should check their protein intake with a doctor or registered dietitian. Nothing here is medical advice.
          </p>
