            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming Whey Tech Pro 24 is an isolate</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The tub says whey protein isolate in large type, but the protein is an isolate and concentrate blend. That is fine for most people and cheaper per gram, but if concentrate bloats you or you want the leanest label, buy the actual Whey Protein Isolate instead.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the 1.5 lb tub at full price</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                At $44.99, the small isolate tubs cost roughly $1.96 to $2.14 per 25 g of protein, no cheaper than certified rivals. The 3 lb and 5 lb tubs, Vitamin Shoppe's 15% Auto Delivery discount and its frequent sales all bring the cost down to about $1.50 to $1.80.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating a quality promise as a certification</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The Vitamin Shoppe says independent labs verify its own brands, but we found no Informed Choice, Informed Sport or NSF listing for BodyTech protein. If you are drug tested, a company quality program does not protect you. Choose a product you can verify in a public registry.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Picking a cereal flavor for a clean label</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Cinnamon Cereal and similar flavors add a sunflower creamer with maltodextrin and modified starch, xanthan gum and acesulfame potassium on top of sucralose. They may taste better, but if you chose BodyTech for a short ingredient list, French Vanilla or Unflavored is the version to buy.
              </p>
