                  The labels we checked list 25 g of protein per scoop in French Vanilla, Rich Chocolate, Unflavored and Cinnamon Cereal, at about 110 calories. Scoop size varies from about 29 g to 33 g by flavor. One Amazon listing for the 3 lb Rich Chocolate tub says 24 g, so check the panel on the exact tub you buy.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Who makes BodyTech protein?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  BodyTech is The Vitamin Shoppe's own brand, along with the BodyTech Elite performance line. It is sold in Vitamin Shoppe stores, on its website and, for the main products, on Amazon. The Vitamin Shoppe does not publicly name the contract manufacturer for each product, which is common for store brands.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is BodyTech third-party tested?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The Vitamin Shoppe says its own brands pass 320 quality checks and that independent labs verify purity and potency. We could not find BodyTech protein in the Informed Choice, Informed Sport or NSF Certified for Sport registries at the time of writing, and found no public lot-level test results. Drug-tested athletes should choose a certified powder such as Dymatize ISO100.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What is the difference between BodyTech Whey Tech Pro 24 and the isolate?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Whey Tech Pro 24 blends whey isolate with whey concentrate, gives 24 g of protein and about 120 calories per scoop, and adds lactase and Aminogen enzymes with sucralose and acesulfame potassium. The isolate is pure isolate with 25 g of protein and about 110 calories. Whey Tech Pro 24 is cheaper per gram; the isolate is leaner and lower in lactose.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is BodyTech cheaper at Amazon or Vitamin Shoppe?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  It depends on the product and the week. The small isolate tubs were the same $44.99 at both when we checked, but Vitamin Shoppe's 15% Auto Delivery and frequent sales made it cheaper there. Whey Tech Pro 24 in 5 lb was cheaper on Amazon, about $1.35 per 25 g against about $1.69. Compare cost per 25 g on the day.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does BodyTech protein have artificial sweeteners?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Most flavors do. French Vanilla and Rich Chocolate isolate use sucralose, Cinnamon Cereal adds acesulfame potassium, and Whey Tech Pro 24 uses both sucralose and acesulfame potassium. The Clear Whey Isolate uses sucralose and stevia. BodyTech Whey Protein Isolate Unflavored contains no sweetener at all, only whey isolate and sunflower lecithin.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

